domain PLAN_RECONSIDERATION:
  description "Reconsider test-authority enablement and cc304 ordering after ADR-0034 acceptance."

problem P1:
  |
    Reorder the next repository work so that it delivers observable safe functionality
    without turning migration exactness or test-passing into the objective.

evidence E1:
  |
    On 2026-09-16 the owner accepted exact ADR0034 revision one and instructed that
    the plan be reconsidered.

evidence E2:
  |
    The owner previously lowered the priority of migration accuracy and strictness,
    described competing approaches as a trial order, and instructed work to proceed
    from a functionally safe option.

evidence E3:
  |
    Current cc304 is one six-point task combining create, revise, migration, owner
    answer and retry, API and UI, worker and provider driver, persistence, several
    recovery scenarios, and three-mode completion evidence.

evidence E4:
  |
    Current test selection discovers 156 unit/deployment/release tests. It classifies
    137 unsealed tests as active ungoverned, 16 inventoried tests as disabled, and
    only 3 inventoried tests as current. ADR0034 requires unsealed tests to be disabled
    as current evidence.

evidence E5:
  |
    The dirty worktree contains an unsealed local revision-scope classifier, tests,
    Ollama adapter, replay script, and three result directories. They are preserved
    WIP but cannot establish a current plan choice under ADR0034.

evidence E6:
  |
    The accepted design and current revision-seven plan already separate candidate
    generation and review from final acceptance, deployment, policy activation, and
    production migration. A controlled provider reply can traverse API or UI, worker,
    driver, persistence and review without a paid call or current-character mutation.

premise VALUE:
  |
    The intended near-term value is an owner-visible working authoring path. More
    migration classification rules, fixtures, or resealed tests do not provide that
    value unless they remove a demonstrated blocker in the selected path.

premise SAFETY:
  |
    The first functional trial must be local, reversible, preserve current character
    state, create only a review candidate, perform no paid call or deployment, and
    keep final acceptance as a separate action.

premise AUTHORITY:
  |
    Only source-matched non-stale verification Seals with explicit Causes can be cited
    as current test evidence. This does not authorize bulk resealing or rewriting
    upstream requirements around tests.

premise OPTIONS:
  |
    Resume cc304 unchanged; first repair or seal the broad historical test suite; or
    establish the ADR0034 selector and then run one bounded revise path through the
    real local boundaries before choosing create and migration extensions from the
    observed result.

decision D1 based_on P1, E1, E2, E3, E4, E5, E6, VALUE, SAFETY, AUTHORITY, OPTIONS:
  |
    Do not resume cc304 unchanged and do not bulk-repair or bulk-seal tests. First
    implement only the ADR0034 selector and its own downstream verification so later
    pass or fail claims have an explicit current basis.

decision D2 based_on D1, E2, E3, E6, VALUE, SAFETY:
  |
    Propose splitting cc304. The first functional slice is one owner-visible revise
    request that produces a non-current review candidate through the real local API or
    UI, worker, controlled provider driver, persistence and semantic diff. It performs
    no final acceptance, paid call, deployment, policy activation, or migration.

decision D3 based_on D2, E2, E5, VALUE:
  |
    Judge the next order from the observed revise result. Extend to create when the
    common route works. Leave migration and its lower-priority exactness work until
    after create and revise expose a concrete remaining need. Preserve the unsealed
    scope experiment only as non-authoritative WIP; do not use its pass counts to
    choose or justify the path.

decision D4 based_on D1, D2, D3, AUTHORITY:
  |
    Seal only verification directly needed for each selected slice after checking its
    exact Cause and source. Do not make aggregate green status, stale-test repair, or
    Seal count a completion criterion. Completion is the observable functional outcome
    plus current evidence for that exact outcome.
